      "every inverse image contains K = Ker(Q), and every quotient object is literally an object of D, giving one side of the ordered correspondence",
      "an isomorphism Q(Y) to Q(X) has a roof with both legs inverted; Categories Tag 05Q9 and Derived Tag 05RL place both legs in S(K)",
      "the two cone triangles and strict fullness propagate membership from Y and K to the roof object and then to X, proving the other side of the correspondence",
      "strict closure changes neither inverse image nor saturation, so the proof covers every full triangulated quotient subcategory rather than only strictly full ones",
      "direct-summand closure is preserved and reflected because the quotient functor is the identity on objects and the ordered correspondence is exact",
      "for a full saturated A containing B, its strict closure contains K by the minimal-saturation lemma, yielding the general saturated-image conclusion",
      "the sole source roof diagram is represented by independently written fraction notation; no source diagram or prose is copied"
